{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>As my master speaks.</b> And it is written: ״את אשר דבר ה' אל עבדים כן נעשה״ — 'that which YHWH spoke to your servants, so we shall do' — meaning that the words of Moses are the words of YHWH, for he is an instrument of the holy spirit, prepared for prophecy at all times and at every hour, and his words are the words of HaShem. Or perhaps they called Moses by the name of the King, for so he is called by His name in another place, as the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded (Exodus 33) on ״והיה כל מבקש ה'״ — 'and everyone who sought YHWH' — it is not written here 'everyone who sought Moses' but rather 'everyone who sought YHWH,' for the one who cleaves is called by the name of Him to whom he cleaves. For this reason the prophets and angels were called by the special Name in several verses of the Torah, and I have already mentioned this several times."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:31.762856850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}